# DeployTool.action
#
# The ROS2-action form of problog_project's DeployTool BT node (see
# module/contracts/schema.yaml's own DeployTool entry). Lowers a tool
# that's ALREADY installed -- currently restricted to tool kind=plow
# only (see tool_action_node.py's own docstring) -- same start/halt
# shape as InstallTool.action, a genuine mirror image reusing the exact
# same fixed-Duration/battery-only-triggers/coin-flip machinery.
#
# Server: amiga_ros2_planners' tool_action_node, which runs this for
# `tool`'s own configured Duration (this problem's own config.yaml,
# tool.deploy.duration_seconds.<kind>), halting early on whichever of
# `triggers` fires first, or resolving a success/failure coin flip
# (tool.deploy.success_probability) once the full Duration elapses with
# nothing halting it early. On success, tool_action_node marks its own
# tracked tool as DEPLOYED -- see move_to_node.py's own note on how
# that changes a SUBSEQUENT MoveTo's speed (tool.equipped.<kind>.
# deployed_speed), and battery_sim_node's own note on how it changes
# moving_drain_rate (tool.equipped.<kind>.deployed_moving_drain_rate).

# The tool INSTANCE id (e.g. "plow1") currently attached -- same id= an
# earlier InstallTool.action goal used. Its own kind must be plow.
string tool

# Same battery-only restriction as InstallTool.action's own triggers port.
string[] triggers
---
# Result

# "deploy_success"/"deploy_failure" if the full Duration elapsed
# (matching InstallTool.action's own bare-reason adaptation of
# schema.yaml's literal deploy_tool_success(Tool,ActionCode) term), or
# the name of whichever battery trigger fired first.
string reason

# true iff reason is "deploy_success".
bool status
---
# Feedback

# Wall-clock seconds elapsed since this action started.
float64 elapsed_s
